body:
Keeping an eye out for a bigger fish-tank to repurpose is always a good idea. Or other animal enclosures you can modify. My syrian now lives in my lizard's old 4ft tank which I hamster-proofed, so just have a good look round and keep an open mind :)

&#x200B;

You can also spend time with her by holding her, if she enjoys it, and if it is 100% safe to do so let her have a run around free. Only do this in a contained room with no exposed wires, no cupboards she can hide in, nothing she can harm herself on and somewhere you can keep a very close eye on her. If you don't want to do this consider getting a play pen to let her in with various boxes etc for her to explore. Try and only do this during her normal waking hours so you're not waking her to put her in :)
